From cc01d777c053ed85db40999ffbe119d0b3a163ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:18:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sign in as the Cartouche Installer does

Since October 2026, Apple refuses a sign-in whose identity is not the
kind of machine that made its anisette data: "-80045" when it starts,
"-80046" after a verification code. SideStore says it is a Mac, but
takes anisette from any server of its list, most of them Android ones,
or makes it on the device; writes the identifier in hexadecimal, which
the v3 servers read as base64 and so turn into another machine; falls
back to a server's own v1 headers, those of another machine still; and
keeps the identifier and adi.pb one server made for the next. A server
that refuses that adi.pb ("-45061 reprovision required") is never asked
for a new one, and the keychain outlives a reinstall, so reinstalling
does not help.

A sign-in now gets anisette as the Cartouche Installer (iloader,
isideload 0.5.2) does, which Apple accepts:

- the Mac the Installer says it is, and the Xcode it says it runs, on
  every request: provisioning, anisette, sign-in, verification code;
- anisette from the Installer's Mac servers only, in its order,
  starting with the one that last worked;
- the identifier in base64, as the v3 protocol has it, and no v1
  headers should /v3/get_headers fail;
- the client-provided data and headers the Installer sends;
- fresh anisette from the same machine once the player has typed a
  verification code;
- the machine kept in the keychain with what it was made with, and made
  again when it was made another way, when the server refuses it, or
  when Apple refused the last sign-in with it, which then starts with
  the next server.

What follows such a sign-in, the developer services and the renewals,
keeps its machine and identity, since Apple's token works only with
them. An account signed in before keeps SideStore's own way until it
signs in again. Network errors with these servers count as anisette in
Cartouche's measurements.

